<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani yarn rates end mixed, seen rising.</title>
<headline>Pakistani yarn rates end mixed, seen rising.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton yarn rates closed mixed on Sunday but are likely to increase because of a sharp rise in the domestic cotton market amid rumours of a pest attack on the cotton crop.</p>
<p>Rates in rupees supplied by the Pakistan Yarn Merchants Association for a 10-lb (4.54 kg) cone of 21 counts:</p>
<p>				     Sunday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Al-Karam (A.K.)	    435	    435</p>
<p>    Baig (Magic)		 420	    425</p>
<p>    Globe (Hina)		 420	    420</p>
<p>($1 = 37.06 rupees) -- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
